course: dictionary
lesson: 13224
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Gander» is one of them. On a farm, a gander is a male goose: «The gander hissed at us from the edge of the pond.»
explain: In everyday talk in Britain and Australia, a gander can also be a quick look. «Come and have a gander at my new drawing!» Nobody is asking for a goose there. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is this sentence about an animal or about looking? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A gander is an adult male goose. The female is a goose, and the young are goslings.
fact: «Have a gander» means have a quick look. It is mostly used in British and Australian English.
fact: «Take a gander» means the same as «have a gander».
fact: The saying «what's good for the goose is good for the gander» means a rule should be fair to both people.
fact: «Informal» means relaxed, everyday talk, not formal writing.
exercise: «The gander stretched his wings and honked at the farm dog.» What is a gander? | A young goose | A kind of farm gate | A female goose | *An adult male goose
exercise: «Come and have a gander at my new bike!» What does have a gander mean? | Give a loud shout | Ride away fast | Fall off the bike | *Have a quick look
exercise: «The goslings followed their mum across the grass.» Who are the goslings? | The male geese | The old hens | *The young geese | The farmer's children
test: In the saying «what's good for the goose is good for the gander», what does it mean? | Only geese can have fun | Ganders always win races | Farm animals should be kept apart | *A rule must be fair to both people
test: «Take a gander at this map before we leave.» What does take a gander mean here? | Take a long walk | Take a photo of a goose | Take the map away | *Take a quick look
exam: Which word means the female goose? | Gander | Gosling | Drake | *Goose
